# Contribute to the docs

This site uses [Middleman](https://middlemanapp.com/) with Markdown pages and one
shared ERB layout. Its dependencies are separate from the catalogue application.
Run these commands from the repository root using the configured Ruby 4.0.9:

```fish
mise exec -- ruby -S bundle install --gemfile docs/site/Gemfile
mise exec -- ruby -C docs/site -S bundle exec middleman server
```

Open [http://localhost:4567](http://localhost:4567). Edit the usage pages under
`docs/site/source/`. The operations page renders `docs/operations.md`, and the
build copies `docs/openapi.yaml` into the output so these contracts keep one
canonical source.

## Build and check the site

```fish
set -gx DOCS_BASE_PATH /release-mirror
mise exec -- ruby -C docs/site -S bundle exec middleman build
mise exec -- ruby docs/site/check_links.rb docs/site/build /release-mirror
```

The static output is `docs/site/build/`. `DOCS_BASE_PATH` defaults to `/` for local
preview; the pipeline supplies the GitHub Pages project path for published
links and stylesheets. The link check verifies generated local links, anchors
and assets without contacting a live catalogue or external website.

## Publish to GitHub Pages

The **Documentation** workflow builds and checks documentation changes on pull
requests. A push of those changes to `main` uploads the checked output and
publishes it through the `github-pages` environment. Pull requests cannot deploy.
You can also dispatch the workflow manually on `main` to republish.

Before the first publication, a repository administrator must select **GitHub
Actions** under **Settings → Pages → Build and deployment → Source**. The workflow
does not enable Pages, configure a custom domain or deploy the catalogue service.
Keep any desired deployment protection rules on the `github-pages` environment.

Documentation builds run for `docs/**` and their workflow changes. Catalogue
verification runs its application jobs only when application inputs change.
The workflows use GitHub path filters to run only for relevant changes. Their
checks are not required by branch protection, so review their results before merging.
